    {
      "id": "content",
      "heading": "Collection Interface",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Collection interface is at the core of Java's collections framework. It serves as the root interface for working with groups of objects, known as elements, and provides the foundation for more specific interfaces like List, Set, and Queue."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Data Structures and Algorithms/Collection Interface/Collection%20Interface/Untitled.png",
          "alt": "Untitled",
          "originalPath": "Collection%20Interface/Untitled.png"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 39,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "key-characteristics-of-the-collection-interface",
      "heading": "Key Characteristics of the Collection Interface",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Purpose: Provides a unified way to manipulate groups of objects.",
            "Hierarchy: Serves as the base interface for all collections (excluding maps).",
            "Generic Support: Uses generics to enforce type safety, ensuring compile-time checks."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 32,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "core-methods-of-the-collection-interface",
      "heading": "Core Methods of the Collection Interface",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Collection interface provides methods for adding, removing, and accessing elements, as well as querying collection properties."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 17,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "commonly-used-methods",
          "heading": "Commonly Used Methods",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Description"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "boolean add(E e)",
                  "Adds an element to the collection. Returns true if successful."
                ],
                [
                  "boolean addAll(Collection<? extends E> c)",
                  "Adds all elements from the specified collection."
                ],
                [
                  "void clear()",
                  "Removes all elements from the collection."
                ],
                [
                  "boolean contains(Object o)",
                  "Checks if the collection contains the specified element."
                ],
                [
                  "boolean containsAll(Collection<?> c)",
                  "Checks if the collection contains all elements in the specified collection."
                ],
                [
                  "boolean isEmpty()",
                  "Checks if the collection is empty."
                ],
                [
                  "Iterator<E> iterator()",
                  "Returns an iterator over the elements in the collection."
                ],
                [
                  "boolean remove(Object o)",
                  "Removes a single instance of the specified element."
                ],
                [
                  "boolean removeAll(Collection<?> c)",
                  "Removes all elements in the collection that are also in the specified collection."
                ],
                [
                  "boolean retainAll(Collection<?> c)",
                  "Retains only elements that are also in the specified collection."
                ],
                [
                  "int size()",
                  "Returns the number of elements in the collection."
                ],
                [
                  "Object[] toArray()",
                  "Converts the collection into an array."
                ],
                [
                  "<T> T[] toArray(T[] a)",
                  "Converts the collection into a typed array."
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 148,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "types-of-collections",
      "heading": "Types of Collections",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Collection interface is extended by other interfaces that specify different collection types."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 13,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "list-interface",
          "heading": "List Interface",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Ordered collection (sequence) that allows duplicate elements.",
                "Examples: ArrayList, LinkedList, Vector"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 11,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "set-interface",
          "heading": "Set Interface",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Unordered collection that does not allow duplicate elements.",
                "Examples: HashSet, LinkedHashSet, TreeSet"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "queue-interface",
          "heading": "Queue Interface",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Represents a collection designed for holding elements prior to processing.",
                "Examples: PriorityQueue, LinkedList"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 13,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
